{"content":[{"c":["SHEPHUPHAM*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Benjamin’s fourth son (called “Muppim” in ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.21","r":"Gen.46.21","rawR":"Gen.46.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.21","value":"Gen.46.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gen 46:21"},") and the father of the Shuphamite family (",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.39","r":"Num.26.39","rawR":"Num.26.39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.39","value":"Num.26.39"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 26:39"},"; see ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," mg). In the corresponding genealogy of Benjamin (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.12","r":"1Chr.7.12","rawR":"1Chr.7.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.12","value":"1Chr.7.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:12"},") he is called Shuppim, appearing as Benjamin’s great-grandson. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Shuppim_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Shuppim_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Shuppim_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Shuppim #1"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Shephuphan_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Shephuphan_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Shephuphan_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Shephuphan"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Shephupham","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gen 46:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.21","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.21","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.21"},{"anchorText":"Nm 26:39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.26.39","rawQueryValue":"Num.26.39","sourceRefExact":"Num.26.39"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.12","rawQu